WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.924 --> 00:00:03.905
Daisy bent down.

2
00:00:04.325 --> 00:00:06.607
A mouse was trembling near her feet.

3
00:00:06.667 --> 00:00:08.929
"Your cat ran past," he said.

4
00:00:09.089 --> 00:00:14.733
"I barely had time to hide!

5
00:00:30.312 --> 00:00:32.774
She climbed that maple tree just ahead."

6
00:00:32.794 --> 00:00:37.798
"This mouse says Dumpling is in that tree."

7
00:00:38.258 --> 00:00:39.899
Daisy pointed to the maple.

8
00:00:39.919 --> 00:00:45.203
"I told you, stop joking around," Kaleem said.

9
00:00:45.223 --> 00:00:46.744
"This is serious!"

10
00:00:51.108 --> 00:00:53.409
Daisy squinted at the top of the maple.

11
00:00:53.429 --> 00:01:01.796
"Dumpling?" "I'm here!"

12
00:01:02.317 --> 00:01:03.137
a voice called.

13
00:01:03.157 --> 00:01:05.698
"But I'm stuck!"

14
00:01:08.079 --> 00:01:09.060
Kaleem gasped.

15
00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:13.922
"It's Dumpling!"

16
00:01:13.962 --> 00:01:16.583
"You mean you heard her too?"

17
00:01:17.023 --> 00:01:18.704
Daisy asked in surprise.

18
00:01:19.824 --> 00:01:20.624
Kaleem nodded.

19
00:01:20.644 --> 00:01:23.146
"Dumpling meows really loudly."

20
00:01:23.166 --> 00:01:26.627
"She wasn't meowing," Daisy said.

21
00:01:26.647 --> 00:01:28.568
"She was talking."

22
00:01:29.948 --> 00:01:31.369
Kaleem ignored Daisy.

23
00:01:31.389 --> 00:01:33.491
"I'm here!

24
00:01:33.831 --> 00:01:34.932
Come down, Dumpling!"

25
00:01:34.952 --> 00:01:37.735
"I can't!"

26
00:01:38.235 --> 00:01:38.976
the cat said.

27
00:01:38.996 --> 00:01:42.098
"I'm good at climbing up.

28
00:01:43.539 --> 00:01:47.042
But I can't figure out how to climb down."

29
00:01:47.062 --> 00:01:50.485
"Look at the branch next to you," Daisy said.

30
00:01:50.505 --> 00:01:52.026
"Walk halfway out.

31
00:01:52.627 --> 00:01:54.388
Then jump down to the next branch."

32
00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:57.791
"Here, kitty!"

33
00:01:58.171 --> 00:01:58.872
Kaleem said.

34
00:01:59.276 --> 00:02:00.236
"Just come to me!"

35
00:02:00.256 --> 00:02:03.697
"I'd do that if I could fly like a bird."

36
00:02:04.137 --> 00:02:05.538
Dumpling sounded grumpy.

37
00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:08.719
"But I'm a cat, remember?"

38
00:02:09.939 --> 00:02:10.899
Daisy laughed.

39
00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:13.940
"Why are you laughing?"

40
00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:15.161
Kaleem asked.

41
00:02:16.261 --> 00:02:19.802
Daisy realized he really couldn't understand Dumpling's words.

42
00:02:20.762 --> 00:02:21.562
"Never mind."

43
00:02:24.083 --> 00:02:26.724
Dumpling began following Daisy's directions.

44
00:02:28.536 --> 00:02:32.659
Once Dumpling was on the lower branch, Daisy kept directing her.

45
00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:38.802
Finally the cat was low enough to jump to the ground.

46
00:02:38.822 --> 00:02:40.463
"Good kitty!"

47
00:02:42.504 --> 00:02:43.785
Kaleem scooped her up.

48
00:02:43.805 --> 00:02:45.846
"You followed my voice."

49
00:02:45.866 --> 00:02:51.630
"If you say so," Dumpling said.

50
00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:55.232
"I'm just happy to be down.

51
00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:58.821
I could use a snack and a nap."

52
00:03:01.082 --> 00:03:03.363
Daisy told Kaleem what the cat had said.

53
00:03:04.363 --> 00:03:05.044
He frowned.

54
00:03:05.984 --> 00:03:07.585
"Why do you keep making this joke?

55
00:03:08.185 --> 00:03:09.185
It's not funny."

56
00:03:09.205 --> 00:03:13.567
"It's not a joke," Daisy said.

57
00:03:16.028 --> 00:03:18.789
As they walked back home, she explained again.

58
00:03:18.809 --> 00:03:21.650
"Everyone knows you're good with animals, Daisy.

59
00:03:22.111 --> 00:03:25.492
But you're not Doctor Dolittle, the guy in that book we read in school."

60
00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:30.343
The Story of Doctor Dolittle was one of Daisy's favorite books.

61
00:03:31.023 --> 00:03:34.306
The main character could talk to all kinds of animals.

62
00:03:36.067 --> 00:03:37.428
And now she could too!

63
00:03:38.128 --> 00:03:39.089
Daisy groaned.

64
00:03:39.109 --> 00:03:42.191
"How can I convince you?

65
00:03:42.211 --> 00:03:46.675
Oh, here's Beatrice, the bee who stung me."

66
00:03:47.535 --> 00:03:50.477
"Tell her not to sting me," Kaleem said nervously.

67
00:03:50.497 --> 00:03:53.780
"She knows you're allergic," Daisy said.

68
00:03:54.644 --> 00:03:56.565
"Wait—does this mean you believe me?"

69
00:03:57.526 --> 00:03:58.947
Kaleem rolled his eyes.

70
00:03:59.767 --> 00:04:06.071
"No!" "Beatrice, I need to convince Kaleem I can talk to animals," Daisy said.

71
00:04:06.091 --> 00:04:08.432
"Would you please fly around my head?"

72
00:04:09.152 --> 00:04:10.233
Beatrice sighed.

73
00:04:10.253 --> 00:04:13.435
"I don't know.

74
00:04:14.215 --> 00:04:15.716
Is that against the rules?"

75
00:04:15.736 --> 00:04:17.837
"What rules?"

76
00:04:18.197 --> 00:04:19.038
Daisy asked.

77
00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:24.092
"Oops! Um, nothing I mean, uh, okay."

78
00:04:26.073 --> 00:04:27.913
Beatrice circled Daisy's head.

79
00:04:29.734 --> 00:04:30.514
Kaleem shrugged.

80
00:04:30.534 --> 00:04:32.534
"That's not really proof.

81
00:04:33.395 --> 00:04:35.055
Bees fly around all the time."

82
00:04:35.755 --> 00:04:37.336
Suddenly Dumpling spoke up.

83
00:04:37.356 --> 00:04:42.297
"Tell him I saw him put on dinosaur underwear this morning."

84
00:04:43.537 --> 00:04:44.598
Daisy giggled.

85
00:04:44.618 --> 00:04:47.378
"Dumpling says you're wearing dinosaur underwear.

86
00:04:47.678 --> 00:04:48.339
Is that true?"

87
00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:53.560
How do you know that?"

88
00:04:54.048 --> 00:04:55.329
Kaleem looked shocked.

89
00:04:55.969 --> 00:04:57.270
Then he looked amazed.

90
00:04:57.290 --> 00:05:00.031
"Did Dumpling really tell you that?

91
00:05:00.751 --> 00:05:02.953
I should have known you would never lie to me, Daisy.

92
00:05:03.653 --> 00:05:05.134
You can talk to animals!"

93
00:05:05.154 --> 00:05:07.795
"That's what I've been trying to tell you!"

94
00:05:08.796 --> 00:05:09.716
Daisy grinned.

95
00:05:09.736 --> 00:05:12.758
"I guess now you can call me Daisy
